    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Points system replacing the level rules\n\n**New `MembershipPoints.of(namesakeCount, email, householdSize, registrationDate)`** \u2014 computes the points total:\n- start at 0\n- +2 when an email is present (non-null, non-blank)\n- +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0\n- +2 when `householdSize` is 3 or more\n- +3 when tenure since `registrationDate` exceeds 365 days\n\n**`MembershipLevel.of(int points)`** \u2014 rewritten to band points into a level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+). The old direct-factor computation is gone.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 now maps both `membershipPoints` (from `MembershipPoints.of`) and `membershipLevel` (from `MembershipLevel.of(MembershipPoints.of(...))`), so responses return both fields.\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 updated to the new API (computes points, then the level for the audit line).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema and corrected the `membershipLevel` description/constraints (now 1\u20134, banded from points), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the new field.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`membershipPoints`=3, `membershipLevel`=2 for a fresh owner with an email and no namesake) passes, and the full suite reports BUILD SUCCESS.",
