    "probe_text": "Here is the full ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. I've marked each entry as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutates/derives state), in exact execution order.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n0. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without this role the whole endpoint is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `RequireOwnerFields`\nInternally, in this order:\n1. **[S]** Normalize the **address** (`OwnerAddress.normalize` \u2014 whitespace collapsed) and write it back onto the request.\n2. **[V]** Reject if any required field is **blank/missing** among `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `MissingFieldsException` (400, lists offending fields). Note the address is checked *after* normalization, so an all-whitespace address counts as missing.\n3. **[S/V]** Normalize **telephone** to E.164 (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`); if it can't form a valid number \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n4. **[S/V]** Normalize **email** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`); may throw `InvalidEmailException`.\n5. **[S]** Publish the normalized body for later steps (so stored/returned/compared values are the normalized forms).\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`\n6. **[V]** If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is **after today**, reject \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent date is allowed. Uses the date as supplied (before business-day roll).\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `RequirePostcode`\n7. **[V]** If a postcode is present, it must be **4 digits** and, for a city with a known region, within that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Absent/blank postcode passes.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `RequireUniqueIdentity` *(transaction begins here)*\n8. **[V]** Scan all existing owners:\n   - **Contact duplicate** \u2014 same `contactKey` (telephone + email) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Not bypassable.\n   - **Household duplicate** \u2014 same `householdId` (same last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409), **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses this check.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `RequireCityCapacity`\n9. **[V]** If the owner's city already has **\u2265 50 owners** (case-insensitive, trimmed) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `RequireDailyRegistrationLimit`\n10. **[V]** Compute the effective **business day** (supplied-or-today, weekends rolled to Monday). If **\u2265 100 owners** already registered on that day \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException` (429).\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n11. **[S]** Map the DTO to an `Owner` entity, then set its `registrationDate` to the **effective business day** (weekend rolled forward to Monday).\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `FlagPossibleDuplicate`\n12. **[S]** Set `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`. A non-hard-duplicate sharing an existing owner's last name + postcode but with a *different* telephone is flagged (lowest matching id wins). A declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) is never flagged.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`\n13. **[S]** Set `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode (falling back to city) and HASH8 is the first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `CountNamesakes`\n14. **[S]** Set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `CountHouseholdMembers`\n15. **[S]** Set `householdSize` = existing members of the same household (last name + postcode) **plus one** for this owner.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `FlagBulkSignupWarning`\n16. **[S]** Set `bulkSignupWarning = true` if **> 80 owners** were already created on the same adjusted business day.\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n17. **[S]** Persist the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns the generated id).\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n18. **[S]** Compute membership points/level and write an `AUDIT` log line: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n## Step 15 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n19. **[S]** Map to `OwnerDto` and respond **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes worth flagging:**\n- Steps 4\u201315 all run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so they commit as a single transaction at the end.\n- The three \"require\" business-rule checks (unique identity, city capacity, daily limit) each do a full `findAll()` scan, and they run *inside* the transaction, unlike the field/date/postcode validations (steps 1\u20133) which run before it.\n- `DataIntegrityViolationException` and a generic `Exception` handler also exist in `officefloor/escalation/`, catching persistence failures at the `SaveOwner` step and anything otherwise unhandled.\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
